{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cice_transport",
  "description": "CICE horizontal transport (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the per-category conservative advection of the default configuration of cesm3_cice6_6_3_22, lowered onto the traced 3x5 subdomain (N_I = 3 T cells along x, N_J = 5 along y, global cells (2..4, 4..8) of the stage-1 dump) with the EarthSciDiscretizations CICE B-grid flux-divergence rule (grids/cice_bgrid/rules/transport_flux_divergence.esm). The Fortran advects the category area (the 'mass' field mm, including open water in category 0) and the per-category tracers with the incremental-remapping scheme of Dukowicz & Baumgardner (2000) / Lipscomb & Hunke (2004) (transport_remap, ice_transport_driver.F90:251-700; horizontal_remap, ice_transport_remap.F90:317-831; construct_fields F90:1009-1283; departure_points F90:1449-1623; transport_integrals F90:3188-3472), and the B-grid velocity is defined at the cell corners (ice_HaloUpdate of uvel/vvel before the remap, ice_transport_driver.F90:430-445). The conservative statement per category n is the continuity system d(a_n)/dt + div(a_n u) = 0, d(v_n)/dt + div(v_n u) = 0, d(vs_n)/dt + div(vs_n u) = 0 for the area aicen, the ice volume per unit area vicen = a_n*h_n, and the snow volume vsnon, together with the energy-conservation forms d(vicen*qicen)/dt + div(vicen*qicen*u) = 0 and d(vsnon*qsnon)/dt + div(vsnon*qsnon*u) = 0 for the layer enthalpies (the Fortran's type-2 tracer transport conserves the tracer*mass product; qicen/qsnon are carried as tracers nt_qice/nt_qsno, ice_transport_driver.F90:98-102). The model writes these as spatial-D rewrite targets (div(c u) = D(c*uvel, x) + D(c*vvel, y)) lowered by the transport_flux_divergence rule to the conservative cell flux divergence of the Fortran's mass update mm(i,j) = mm(i,j) - w1*tarear(i,j) with w1 = mflxe(i,j) - mflxe(i-1,j) + mflxn(i,j) - mflxn(i,j-1) (ice_transport_remap.F90:3586-3590) and the centered edge reconstruction of edgearea_e/n (F90:658-666): the rule's face average (uS+uN)/2*(cL+cR)/2*HTE per edge, divided by tarea, is the continuous flux form that the incremental-remapping scheme replaces with the departure-cell integrals -- the scheme difference is documented in README.md and quantified by the pin tolerances of the two tests below (integrated-pin residuals aicen <= 3.04e-5, vicen <= 3.33e-5, vsnon <= 1.78e-4 relative). The two enthalpy-tracer equations are documented but not carried as model equations: their product-form LHS cannot define an unknown under the esm equation-balance rule, and the tracer fields are parameters fed by the thermodynamics states (the assembly wires Thermodynamics.qicen -> Transport.qicen by param_to_var). The velocity and grid fields are parameters overridden from the dumps in the tests: uvel/vvel are the transport dump's t_entr step-1 ncat-1 rows (the cell (i,j) row carries the U(i,j) NE-corner velocity = the post-dynamics field), HTE/HTN/tarea are derived from the stress-dump metrics (HTE = (3*cyp - cym)/4, HTN = (3*cxp - cxm)/4, tarea = dxT*dyT). Import contract: the model declares the N_I/N_J/NCAT/N_ILYR/N_SLYR metaparameters and the i/j/ncat/ice_layer/snow_layer index sets locally (the esm CLI 0.4.0/0.6.0 rejects faq-range metaparameter references when a template library is imported with bindings -- RangeSpec round-trip parse bug of the esm CLI), and imports the flux-divergence rule by reference from the EarthSciDiscretizations library (${ESD_ROOT} must be set to that repo's checkout when running the tests).",
  "license": "MIT",
   "tags": [
    "cryosphere",
    "sea-ice",
    "cice",
    "transport",
    "advection",
    "cesm"
   ],
   "created": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z",
   "authors": [
    "EqESM project contributors"
   ],
   "references": [
    {
     "citation": "Hunke, E. C., Allard, R., Bailey, D. A., Blain, P., Craig, A., Dupont, F., ... & Roberts, A. F. (2023). CICE-Consortium Icepack v1.2.4 and CICE v6.3.22: documentation and user's guide. Los Alamos National Laboratory (LA-UR-23-31851)."
    },
    {
     "citation": "Dukowicz, J. K., & Baumgardner, J. R. (2000). Incremental remapping as a transport/advection algorithm. Journal of Computational Physics, 160(1), 318-335."
    },
    {
     "citation": "Lipscomb, W. H., & Hunke, E. C. (2004). Modeling sea ice transport using incremental remapping. Monthly Weather Review, 132(6), 1341-1354."
    },
    {
     "citation": "CESM (Community Earth System Model), ESCOMP/CESM: CICE sea-ice source (cesm3_cice6_6_3_22) - ice_transport_driver.F90, ice_transport_remap.F90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
     "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CESM"
    },
    {
     "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
     "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
    }
   ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "N_I": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 3,
   "description": "number of T cells along the B-grid x axis of the traced subdomain (global cells 2..4 of the stage-1 dump), [-]"
  },
  "N_J": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 5,
   "description": "number of T cells along the B-grid y axis (global cells 4..8 of the dump), [-]"
  },
  "NCAT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 5,
   "description": "number of ice thickness categories (namelist ncat = 5), [-]"
  },
  "N_ILYR": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 8,
   "description": "number of ice layers (D-class namelist nilyr = 8), [-]"
  },
  "N_SLYR": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 3,
   "description": "number of snow layers (D-class namelist nslyr = 3), [-]"
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "i": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_I"
  },
  "j": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_J"
  },
  "ncat": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NCAT"
  },
  "ice_layer": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_ILYR"
  },
  "snow_layer": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_SLYR"
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "Transport": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cice_bgrid/rules/transport_flux_divergence.esm"
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "aicen": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice area fraction per category, the transported area state: d(aicen)/dt + div(aicen*u) = 0 (the Fortran 'mass' field mm of horizontal_remap, ice_transport_remap.F90:279-280, including category 0 open water), [-]"
    },
    "vicen": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice volume per unit grid-cell area per category vicen = aicen*hin, the transported volume state: d(vicen)/dt + div(vicen*u) = 0, [m]"
    },
    "vsnon": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "snow volume per unit grid-cell area per category vsnon = aicen*hsn, the transported snow-volume state: d(vsnon)/dt + div(vsnon*u) = 0, [m]"
    },
    "div_flux": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "1/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "the conservative per-category flux divergence div_flux = D(c*uvel,x) + D(c*vvel,y) lowered by the transport_flux_divergence rule (the continuous flux form the incremental-remapping scheme replaces; ice_transport_remap.F90:658-666, 3586-3590), the algebraic rewrite target the continuity equations consume, [1/s]"
    },
    "div_flux_v": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "the conservative ice-volume-flux divergence D(vicen*uvel,x) + D(vicen*vvel,y) (the rule target of the vicen continuity equation), [m/s]"
    },
    "div_flux_s": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j",
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "the conservative snow-volume-flux divergence D(vsnon*uvel,x) + D(vsnon*vvel,y) (the rule target of the vsnon continuity equation), [m/s]"
    },
    "qicen": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "ice_layer"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice layer enthalpy tracer (nt_qice, ice_transport_driver.F90:98-102), advected in the product-conservative form d(vicen*qicen)/dt + div(vicen*qicen*u) = 0 (the Fortran's type-2 tracer transport conserves the tracer*mass product); the tracer equation is documented in the model description and deferred to stage 3 (the product-form LHS cannot define an unknown under the esm equation-balance rule), so the field is carried here as a parameter wired from the thermodynamics component's state, [J/m3]"
    },
    "qsnon": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "snow_layer"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "snow layer enthalpy tracer (nt_qsno), advected in the product-conservative form d(vsnon*qsnon)/dt + div(vsnon*qsnon*u) = 0; carried as a parameter wired from the thermodynamics component (see qicen), [J/m3]"
    },
    "uvel": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "x-component of the ice velocity at the B-grid corner points (the transport dump's t_entr step-1 ncat-1 rows: the cell (i,j) row carries the U(i,j) NE-corner velocity = the post-dynamics field, wired from the dynamics component in the assembly), [m/s]"
    },
    "vvel": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "y-component of the ice velocity at the B-grid corner points (wired from the dynamics component), [m/s]"
    },
    "HTE": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "east edge length of the T cell, derived from the stress-dump metrics as HTE = (3*cyp - cym)/4 (the free-name metric of the transport_flux_divergence rule; the tests override it from the dump), [m]"
    },
    "HTN": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "north edge length of the T cell, HTN = (3*cxp - cxm)/4, [m]"
    },
    "tarea": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ],
     "units": "m^2",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "area of the T cell, tarea = dxT*dyT (ice_grid.F90:682; the tests override it from the dump), [m2]"
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "div_flux",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "aicen",
           "uvel"
          ]
         }
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
       },
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "aicen",
           "vvel"
          ]
         }
        ],
        "wrt": "y"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "div_flux_v",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "vicen",
           "uvel"
          ]
         }
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
       },
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "vicen",
           "vvel"
          ]
         }
        ],
        "wrt": "y"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "div_flux_s",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "vsnon",
           "uvel"
          ]
         }
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
       },
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "vsnon",
           "vvel"
          ]
         }
        ],
        "wrt": "y"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "aicen"
      ],
      "wrt": "t"
     },
     "rhs": {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       "div_flux"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "vicen"
      ],
      "wrt": "t"
     },
     "rhs": {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       "div_flux_v"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "vsnon"
      ],
      "wrt": "t"
     },
     "rhs": {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       "div_flux_s"
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "cice_transport_remap_35_integrated",
     "description": "Integrated pin of the traced step-1 transport over [0, 3600] s: the continuity system is integrated from the transport dump's t_entr state (the initial_conditions aicen/vicen/vsnon) with the dump's velocity and grid parameters (uvel/vvel = the t_entr step-1 ncat-1 rows; HTE/HTN/tarea from the stress-dump metrics), and the exit state at local cell (2,4) = global (3,7), t = 3600, is asserted against the dump's t_exit state. The pin is NOT exact: the model integrates the continuous flux form with the rule's centered face-average edge reconstruction (edgearea_e/n, ice_transport_remap.F90:658-666), while the Fortran integrates the incremental-remapping departure-cell integrals, so the residuals quantify the scheme difference (O(C*DeltaC)): aicen rel <= 3.04e-5, vicen rel <= 3.33e-5, vsnon rel <= 1.78e-4 over the five categories, hence the per-assertion tolerances rel 1e-4 / 1e-4 / 2e-4 (the transport_35.py scratch analysis of /scratch.local/ctessum/cice_verify; the entry-to-exit change is ~3e-4..5.5e-4 relative, so the scheme residual is ~10% of the transported change). The expected values are the dump's t_exit rows for cell (3,7).",
